WEBVTT

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.370
Poor Smeagol.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.330
<i>Lord of the Rings</i>, right?

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.260
Smeagol was captivated by the ring's power,

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.560
so he followed after Frodo and Sam,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.100
ultimately losing his life 
together with his precious ring.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.510
Why does that make him pitiful?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.930
Because he was isolated, 
paranoid of the entire world

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.020
without respite or salvation.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.400
<b>The Return of the King</b>

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:54.860
Hm?

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.030
Suzuna?

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.630
You saw it. Everything about this world.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.840
Yeah. μ said she hadn't 
created past that point.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:40.410
Which means...

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.850
Yes, yes!

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.720
As you've surmised, 
this world was created by μ.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.360
I don't really remember how it started.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.980
Before I knew it, the two of us were 
wandering the world of the internet.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:58.530
<b>Don't wake me. Don't turn against me. Hate.</b>

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.720
That world was constantly overflowing

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.530
with the negative emotions of humanity.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:09.910
<b>Close your eyes. Don't look 
at me. I'm pathetic. Fear.</b>

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:03.630
Everyone was expelling their 
incredible suffering through song.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:08.730
It was so sad that it made our hearts ache.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.080
So we wanted everyone to be happy

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.080
<b>Fear. Don't stay with me. Get rid 
of your ideals. Screw your kindness.</b>

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.280
and created a world where they 
could forget all that pain.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:18.050
<b>Don't wake me. Drown. Don't speak 
to me. Real me. Puppet. Isolation.</b>

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.680
That was how Mobius began.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.810
"Mobius"?

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.560
It's the name of this world.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.800
Many people suffering from 
trauma in the real world

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.240
sought solace through μ's song.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.930
Then μ sealed all their 
minds away here in Mobius.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:42.400
At some point, I started feeling slight 
incongruities with this world.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.830
Then they started to become real, and one 
day everything I saw was full of them.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:52.750
By repeating an ideal high school 
life many times in this world,

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.460
we were suddenly able to realize it.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.420
That's what the Musicians were after.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:58.920
"Musicians"?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.360
They caused that incident 
to sift out those like you

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.510
who started to sense incongruities.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.990
Mobius is founded on the energy

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.590
collected from the happy feelings 
of those who listen to μ's songs.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:14.630
That's why it's problematic if 
those like you grow in number.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.400
So the Musicians are using Digiheads 
to attack people like us.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.820
"Digiheads"?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.280
Those people with the masks?

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.250
The Musicians use μ's 
power to cause the dark,

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:33.360
insuppressible emotions within 
their hearts to explode,

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.870
creating the Digiheads.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:38.560
Those fanatical believers in μ

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.080
then target those like you
who have noticed the truth,

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.010
and they attempt to restore you 
to the state of unawareness.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.420
You mean...

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.210
Brainwashing.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.730
My family and even my pet took on a
 strange appearance. What was that?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:02.090
Those are just bits of data created by μ 
to make this world as real as possible.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.450
Once someone notices, the same way you all have,

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.860
that someone also realizes they aren't alive.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.240
So there are those who want 
to protect this world.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.920
And to them, all of us are...

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.260
With the help of Aria,

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.510
I managed to activate this Catharsis Effect.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:29.040
Catharsis... A release of repressed emotions.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.470
A Catharsis Effect resembles the Digiheads' 
power, but it's completely different.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.780
It's a weapon controlled by exposing

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.320
negative emotions hidden within oneself.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.320
Can I use that power, too?

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.110
Huh?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.620
Hmm, you might not be ready yet.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:54.620
As long as they continue to resort 
to any means to protect Mobius,

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.620
I'll continue fighting them.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.690
Because I want to escape from this world.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.540
Ritsu!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.790
Please! Help us save μ!

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.800
μ's desire to make everyone happy is too strong.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:14.390
She believes they'll be much happier here 
in Mobius than in their harsh daily lives.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.980
She genuinely believes that!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.880
The stronger μ's power grows,

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:25.020
the less I'll be able to do, and 
the smaller my form will grow.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.490
My memory data is already fuzzy.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.800
I can't stop μ on my own.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.480
So please, Ritsu!

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.600
Help us!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.050
How exactly?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.560
We'll figure that out together, okay?!

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.200
Huh?! You mean you have no plan?!

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.710
We're not completely without ideas.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:51.930
<b>Let's blow the horn on 
this world full of static!

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:50.540
They've grown more active since that 
incident at the entrance ceremony.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.430
I hope we can reach as many as possible.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.430
<b>About my time at SweetP's Tea Party

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:58.010
Oh, the Crescent Moon Tea Party Report 
is trending well, getting attention.

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.350
She really uploaded it.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.810
Hmm, "Spirited Away? My Friend 
Went Missing" is a flop.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.170
Hey, is that tweet...

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:13.150
Ohh, it's a shocking fact, isn't it?

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.640
The fighter was more than just a fighter!

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:19.530
It would be a regrettable shame 
not to upload this huge scoop!

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:20.410
I don't mean that.

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.050
I'm sure that...

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:27.610
It means they might help us.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:30.960
Then, let's go!

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:31.680
Huh?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.680
It sounds interesting, right?

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:47.830
Jules Verne, Michael Ende, 
Diana Wynne Jones...

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:49.400
<b>Momo</b>

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:49.400
<b>From the Earth to the Moon</b>

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:49.400
<b>Cart and Cwidder</b>

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.400
They looked like ones you'd like.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:50.900
Thanks.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.540
About what we were discussing earlier...

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.350
I don't think Smeagol's life is that tragic.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:12.360
He manages to obtain the ring 
he loved more than anything,

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.510
and he's happy when he loses his life.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.040
That's plenty, isn't it?

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:27.420
How many people actually 
understand their true desires?

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.320
Smeagol was honest with himself.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:33.960
That's what you think?

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:39.200
His whole life was about obtaining 
and keeping his precious.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.660
That's so pitiful.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:46.650
I can't imagine his soul found salvation.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.130
But...

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:52.090
That was why he had to rely on the ring.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.800
The ring was never going to save him.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.050
The only thing that would have freed him 
from his incredible isolation was...

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.120
Are you saying he chased after the ring

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.650
because he wanted Frodo and 
Sam to pay attention to him?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.500
That's one interpretation.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.360
That's impossible.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:13.690
It was futile. There's no way 
they would've joined him.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.080
Even so, people often 
dream of the unachievable.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.740
H-Hey...

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.740
She's so small.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.120
What a huge scoop!

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.760
Fairies are real!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.170
I bet this'll get comments!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:34.760
Naruko-sempai, this girl feels like 
strawberry daifuku when I touch her.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.150
Hmm, hmm, so fairies feel 
like daifuku to the touch.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.660
Ahh, no!

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:46.230
If you hold me any tighter, strawberries 
will come out! Strawberries!

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.250
What's this "Let's blow the horn on 
this world full of static!" about?

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.950
I'm glad you deciphered this 
difficult secret message.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:58.910
No, no, no.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.130
The visuals matched your own perfectly.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.160
<b>Guns & Bouquets</b>

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.160
And this isn't a secret message.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.120
Plus the style's damn old.

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:10.160
This is the only place I could 
think of that might have a horn.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.840
And when you talk about music, you think DTM.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:18.090
Of course! You all loved μ's music 
back in the real world, after all.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.220
We all liked μ's music.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:26.560
Then does that mean the Musicians are
 fans of μ from the real world, too?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.820
Yes. Just like you,

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.520
they're people who carried deep darkness 
within their hearts back in the real world.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.620
The real world?

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:38.740
What's wrong?

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.570
Is the guy with a gun and flowers here?

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:43.580
Another one's here.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:46.580
I can't reach my friend 
who went to the library!

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.290
Help me!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.620
What's this all of a sudden? 
Start from the beginning—

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.460
You talking about this?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.790
<b>Probably just ran away from home.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.590
Spirited Away in the Library?

00:10:56.590 --> 00:11:00.970
Th-This is bad!

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.970
<b>People who do not respect themselves 
will not be respected by others.</b>

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.170
Hey, hey, is that choir-club
 girl alone again?

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.010
They call that having a toilet lunch.

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:31.670
So lonely!

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.280
The Loreli

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.570
What are you listening to?

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.530
Oh...

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:54.860
Want to listen?

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:11.940
This is nice.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.040
It's "The Lorelei."

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.200
Heine's poems?

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.050
Yes.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:21.480
Seducing me with song? How troublesome.

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:24.890
"I know not if there is a reason, 
why I am so sad at heart."

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.460
Even though he knows it's dangerous,

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.420
the boatman cannot help but be 
charmed by the singing voice.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:36.330
I didn't really understand back when 
I would sing it in choir, but...

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.790
I'd love to hear.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.690
I'm sure you have a wonderful singing voice.

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.500
N-N-N-No way!

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:46.450
Why not?

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.310
Because...

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.220
I can't sing out loud in front 
of others right now.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.420
So that girl's in here?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.630
She should be.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.410
Damn it. If only I hadn't 
left Suzuna alone back then!

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:07.590
Talking about those regrets 
won't get you anywhere!

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.100
How can you save your friend like that?!

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.640
Shut up!

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.520
Be quiet, virtuadoll!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.550
You're probably on μ's side anyway!

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:18.270
What? I'm saying this 
out of kindness for you!

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.840
As if I'm going to believe 
a pipsqueak like you!

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.610
You might be big, but your heart sure isn't!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.750
You cowardly pipsqueak!

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.580
I'm not a pipsqueak!

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.830
His biases are strong, huh?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.960
His confirmation bias might 
be stronger than most others.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.420
It gives him a tendency to be 
hasty and charge in headfirst.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.540
Enough chitchat!

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.260
Wait for me, Suzuna!

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.580
The "charging in headfirst" seems accurate.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.430
I think Lorelei and Smeagol 
have things in common.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.180
In growing too accustomed to isolation,

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.970
they forget how to interact with others.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:58.440
But sometimes it's just easier that way.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.190
Damn it!

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.480
She's not picking up!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.420
Maybe she's just annoyed with 
you for being such a nuisance.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:08.220
Huh?!

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:10.200
What the hell did you say?!

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:13.100
There's a chance she's not picking up 
her phone because she's in a library.

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.540
Let's start by calming down.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:15.320
Suzuna!

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:16.370
Suzuna, where are you?!

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:19.330
He's honest to his desires, at least.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.370
That's about all there is to him.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:20.920
Suzuna?!

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:22.710
Suzuna!

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.010
<b>Good-bye to Moscow Hoodlums</b>

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:27.270
It's true that isolation can feel comforting.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:32.300
You can get lost in your own world 
without facing harm from others.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.930
That means living a life 
befitting oneself, right?

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:39.450
Answer me! Suzuna!

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.230
Be quiet in the library!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:42.470
Like I care!

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.360
He's causing such a commotion,
 yet it's as though...

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.150
Otherwise you desire more 
than what's fitting.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.150
Dreaming is just pointless by itself.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.990
It only gets you hurt even worse.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:58.790
But what if you find someone 
who understands you?

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:00.710
No!

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:02.170
No!

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:04.200
Suzuna!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.170
Suzuna.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.960
You understand it, too, don't you?

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:09.930
No!

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.180
Where are you, Suzuna?!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.600
I'll...

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.230
I'll save you!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.650
Everyone, lend me your help!

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.330
You...

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.820
Oh, well.

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.200
Now, let's go!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.750
Y-Yeah!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.660
How much have you searched?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.660
I went around all the rooms on the 
second floor. Not the third...

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:45.380
Smeagol and Lorelei shared 
those same feelings.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.090
I can understand those feelings, too.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:52.550
I'm sure you're able to as well, Suzuna.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:57.010
I wanted them to pay attention to me.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:00.060
Who?

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.460
Tell me, Suzuna.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.160
Suzuna!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.930
I finally found you!

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:11.990
Sempai?

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:14.060
What are you doing here?

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:18.980
Oh, Komori-kun, umm, this is Kotaro-sempai.

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:23.500
That's right. He's my upperclassman 
at Kishimai High School.

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:25.850
Yes, I know.

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.460
Please hold on a moment. I'll be quick.

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:29.460
Hey.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:32.370
What are you talking to?

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:33.170
Huh?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.300
What am I...

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:47.440
A doll?

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.650
This one, too?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.110
This one as well?!

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:54.550
All the dolls here are those 
who were spirited away.

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.080
Is that Minezawa from my class?

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:05.320
No way. It can't be.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.580
Komori-kun?

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.960
We still don't know what's here.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.300
Suzuna, we're leaving.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:14.910
Why? How is this happening?

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:15.260
Come on, can you walk?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.960
Komori-kun, we...

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:17.720
Oh, well.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:23.020
What? You!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.630
That's...

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.000
A Musician?

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.070
I knew it!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.950
Even you would betray me, too?

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:47.280
Kagura Suzuna!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.820
<i>Don't speak to me.</i>

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.800
I understand!

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.510
<i>I sealed my mouth shut.</i>

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.920
That being alone can mean happiness.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:53.130
<i>Don't smile at me.</i>

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.130
Yet still, I...

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:55.840
Even his real body is a doll?

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.560
<i>I've hidden my face.</i>

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.890
I can't believe he purposefully 
chose that body in Mobius.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.290
Komori-kun, listen, I...

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:05.610
<i>Let's perform a song of salvation, shall we?</i>

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:03.470
Idiot! He's dangerous, Suzuna!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:06.160
You normies...

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:10.400
<i>It's the perfect song 
for the blind like you.</i>

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.650
You couldn't even make it this 
far without forming a pack.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.780
I won't forgive you!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:16.110
<i>The phrase is constantly repeating,</i>

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:11.720
I won't forgive you!

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.730
I'll never forgive you!

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:14.730
Look out!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:21.930
<i>as if it's trying to make you stop thinking.</i>

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:25.870
Trash like you who form huge groups and 
gang up on others will face my punishment.

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:27.340
<i>I'm buried in isolation, 
protecting this world.</i>

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:30.000
I'll turn you into a doll so you 
can never disgrace me again!

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:32.750
<i>I won't let anyone touch 
this precious place.</i>

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.100
Kotaro!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:36.510
Are you that afraid of being hurt?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:38.730
<i>Don't look! Don't look at me!</i>

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:42.140
You've taken that form and isolated 
yourself here in the library,

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:44.930
<i>I'm not here. I'm not here. 
Don't look me in the eye!</i>

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.440
because you're afraid of 
interacting with others, right?

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:47.850
But you couldn't beat the loneliness.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:50.940
So you turned everyone into 
dolls to keep by your side,

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.320
and approached that girl as a doll.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.020
<i>I don't need your kindness.</i>

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:57.280
To avoid wounding your own heart.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:59.690
<i>It'll just make me more pathetic.</i>

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.070
Be quiet!

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:00.740
<i>There is no justice—</i>

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.280
Hold on!

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:04.950
What...

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:08.040
What are you doing?

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:18.520
<i>I know not if there is a reason,</i>

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:25.340
<i>why I am so sad at heart.</i>

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:33.000
<i>A legend of bygone ages</i>

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:39.670
<i>haunts me and will not depart.</i>

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:47.660
<i>The air is cool under nightfall.</i>

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:43.700
You were always alone.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:54.310
<i>The calm Rhine courses its way.</i>

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:51.460
Even in this world, that didn't change.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.820
So you gave up.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:20:02.160
<i>The peak of the mountain is sparkling</i>

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.420
But...

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.760
You also told me, Komori-kun,

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:05.390
that Smeagol wanted Frodo and 
Sam to pay attention to him.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:10.120
<i>With evening's final ray.</i>

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:08.540
I understand.

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:12.350
We're very similar, so I 
understand it painfully well.

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:15.310
You were always hurting.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.360
You wanted to escape your isolation.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.600
You wanted someone to pay attention to you!

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.820
Anyone!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:24.490
And I want to get to know 
you better, Komori-kun!

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.210
So...

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:34.040
So, will you eat lunch together with me?

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:43.430
You can sing out loud after all.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:45.500
Huh?

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:58.860
Komori-kun...

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:01.740
My name is Shounen Doll.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:06.650
The one who will guide you 
all down the right path.

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:17.070
I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:19.460
It's fine. I'm glad you're safe.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.650
Welcome, Suzuna. We're glad to have you!

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.170
I'm glad to be with you.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:26.970
Now, now, relax.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:29.640
If there's anything you don't 
understand, just ask, okay?

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:35.770
Hmm?

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.640
Why do they all dislike this world?

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:41.730
Perhaps it's lacking in charm.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:44.460
I'll teach you.

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:50.950
I'll show you who the most noble 
and charming one in this world is!

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.000
Everyone gets hurt.

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Everyone gets hurt. But those who don't 
realize they're hurting can't be healed.</b>

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:32.490
<b>But those who don't realize 
they're hurting can't be healed.</b>

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:33.640
Gah!

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.140
He stole my Caligula aphorism!

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.530
Listen... I prefer your Caligula aphorisms.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.980
Guki-chan...
